A||N||14||Xtreme Fiero's||My "new" 2.5 sucks!!!!||||11||
Z||000000||Xtreme Fiero's||08-15-2000||06:07 PM||||<BR>Ok I just got all the wires/Fuseable links fixed on my new (to me) 2.5L Iron Duke, It is the slowest piece of junk I ever drove!! It wll sit & idle great (slight miss) it seems happy to rev all the way to near redline, I think the problem is timing if I let it sit for to long it will flood out and die. When I try to drive the car first geat is fine when i shift to 2nd it will miss very badly and anything but about 20% throttle, when I shift to 3rd it is worse and I can only give it about 10-15% of full throttle and in 4th if I hold the car @ about 10-15% throttle it will run fine but if I give it any more gas at all it will miss so bad that i slow down. is it timing? or fuel. I am stumped.||||reg||11
Z||000001||sloGT||08-15-2000||06:54 PM||||I had one do that that,and it turned out to be the rotor button.just a thought.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Xtreme Fiero's||08-15-2000||07:16 PM||||OK i just retarded the timing a bit and it runs much better BUT the car will stil cut out if I floor it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"> I'm starting to think that my TPS took a dump in me.<P> OGRE: Can the TPS "fail" only in a few throttle angles? You seem to know alot about the sensors on our cars. Just thought you might be able to shed some light on the subject.||||reg||1
Z||000003||2FAST4U||08-15-2000||11:35 PM||||Is this the same Duke you supposidly fed 200 HP of Nitrous to?||||reg||1
Z||000004||Raydar||08-16-2000||12:11 AM||||Check the plug wires. Make sure none of them are cross-firing.<P>Seems like I've heard of TPSs getting "flat spots" (actually, poor contact) at different places. It works like a volume control on a radio. Ever heard one of those get "scratchy"? <P>Sorry to hear that the other Duke fragged itself. Sounded like an interesting experiment.<p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 08-16-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||Xtreme Fiero's||08-16-2000||12:31 AM||||<BR>2FAST4U: NO this is the engine that has replaced that one.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Mattsfiero||08-16-2000||12:44 AM||||Not to sound Like an Idiot But I had the same problem with mine when I first got it...I gave it a tune up and now she is running at the top of her class....Is it firing properly or is it getting really loud when you step on the gas...if it is getting loud check your wires and firing order you may be missing a spark somewhere...<P>Matt||||reg||1
Z||000007||trigger||08-16-2000||09:27 AM||||My 88 4cyl coupe did exactly the same thing, automatic though.  It turned out to be a fractured spark plug.  I went to put the socket on it to take it out.  Something didn't feel right, I picked up the socket and I was holding the top half of the plug.  I also changed the plug wires when I did this.  They were fairly new but had a little cut in the boot.  They have a lifetime warranty.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Honestly officer, I was just keeping up with the flow of traffic.  I know there aren't any cars in the area, that's how far behind I am.||||reg||1
Z||000008||triker||08-16-2000||10:36 AM||||Plug wires.  They tend to 'leak' under load, so your engine will run ok in nuet and in the lower gears, but will crap out as you load it.||||reg||1
Z||000009||theogre||08-16-2000||11:14 AM||||Yes, TPS can spot fail. I'd replace it AFTER setting the timing to spec. A screwy MAP can also cause such problems. MAP is used to calculate Vacuum Advance curves. Make sure the MAP line is clear, sealed and on the correct TBI port..||||reg||1
Z||000010||Xtreme Fiero's||08-16-2000||11:42 AM||||can I get the TPS off of my parts car or do I need a NEW one? also the car seems to run rich but there are no O2 or Rich fuel mix codes being sent the BUT i don't know if the light is messed up like my tach, fuel and Voltmeter. is there a way to check the "Check Engine" light? if I turn the key to "on" sould the light be on?||||reg||1
Z||000011||Phil||08-16-2000||01:13 PM||||Yep, engine should come on during bulb check||||reg||1
Z||000012||HugGRRRFiero||08-16-2000||01:38 PM||||Yep, The check engine light should turn on with the key in the ON position.<P>  Agree could be a cracked plug, bad wire, or crossfire, make sure all your vacuum lines are good too if you haven't already.<P>  Are you looking to try the NOS setup on this one?<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/huggrrr.gif">  <BR>  <A HREF="mailto:HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com">HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com</A> ||||reg||1
